# PROF-03 soak-harness self-test fixture — scripts/harness/fixtures/soak-selftest-leak.patch
#
# WHAT THIS IS: a planted, deliberate control-plane leak. It makes every
# session launch that reaches dispatchAssignStartWithTopology (the function
# every successful launch passes through, control-plane/internal/session/
# launcher.go) retain 1MiB of heap and leak one goroutine that never exits.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS: scripts/harness/run-soak-profile.sh + scripts/harness/lib/soak_report.py are a
# leak DETECTOR — the only way to trust a detector is to prove it fires on a
# known-bad input. This patch is that known-bad input: apply it, rebuild the
# control-plane image, run a short soak, and confirm cp_goroutines and
# cp_heap_inuse_bytes both come back LEAK in the report. See
# docs/profiling-soak.md "Self-test procedure" for the exact steps.
#
# THIS MUST NEVER LAND APPLIED ON develop OR main. It exists ONLY as this
# fixture file, applied transiently on a throwaway branch, then reverted
# (`git checkout -- control-plane/internal/session/launcher.go`) before that
# branch is discarded. Do not open a PR with this patch applied.
#
# Verified 2026-07-31 in the profiling-campaign-milestone-16 worktree:
#   git apply --check scripts/harness/fixtures/soak-selftest-leak.patch   # clean
#   git apply scripts/harness/fixtures/soak-selftest-leak.patch
#   (cd control-plane && go build ./...)                              # succeeds
#   git checkout -- control-plane/internal/session/launcher.go        # revert
#
